{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/252814-5-rpgs","id":252814,"title":"5 RPGs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-08T18:14:59-07:00","id":252814,"title":"5 RPGs","content":"So you are only allowed to own five RPG core books. No supplements, nothing but the core. What 5 can you not live without?<br /> Here's mine:<br /> 1. VtM 20th anniversary edition. The definitive RPG of my gaming life. Excellent game plus TONS of nostalgia.<br /> 2. Deadlands, any edition. Played the absolute hell out of this, including a Weird West A-Team style game.<br /> 3. Shadowrun...maybe 5e, not sure. Lots of nostalgia here.<br /> 4. Eclipse Phase: never played, but love the universe<br /> 5. Hunter the Vigil: absolute favorite nWoD game, hands down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T19:15:55-07:00","id":252881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/252814-5-rpgs#post252814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Shadowrun...maybe 5E.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_B8FYbTJzsk\" data-code=\"_B8FYbTJzsk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_B8FYbTJzsk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T22:30:15-07:00","id":253025,"title":"","content":"But Chewy, Hunter the Vigil is a supplement!<br /> <br /> Anyway in no particular order<br /> <br /> REIGN<br /> Mutants and Masterminds<br /> Fate<br /> World of Darkness<br /> And maybe Dungeons and Dragons 5, I haven't taken a close enough look at it to make up my mind if I want to give the old grey mare another try.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T02:27:21-07:00","id":253166,"title":"","content":"o0 how..do i choose...this was so hard i spent way to long thinking on it today!<br /> <br /> (These are by no means in order)<br /> <br /> 1.Exalted 2ed (Its fun flaws and all to me! Though lack of errata may be uh a headache but i have most of that shit memorized...who needs supplements when you know it wel enough to make characters for other splats without the books present &gt;&gt;)<br /> 2.Pathfinder (Its a nice base game, but the options to create whole worlds etc make this a high on my list game..cause even without supplements theres SO MUCH crap to do with it)<br /> 3.Dark Hersey (Grimmmmdarrkkkkk love it....cant live without it every now and then) (edited this cause I put &quot;warhammer 40k when i meant to put an actual book title XD )<br /> 4.Demon the fallen (This game... i dont know WHY i love it so much, actually to be more precise I cannot put it into words, but I would burn every RPG book I own to keep it)<br /> 5. Vampire the masqurade 20th (it was what introduced me to rpgs and has a fond place in my heart)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","user":"Scelesta","date":". 09-09-2014, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T04:02:08-07:00","id":253208,"title":"","content":"So many to choose from...<br /> <br /> 1. Exalted! I just love me them pretty shiny Exalted all dressed up and everywhere to go. Granted, I would probably glue all my books together and claim it was a single massive core rulebook.<br /> 2. Mage. I weep tears of joy whenever I think of the epic paradox backlashes I have inflicted upon my gaming group throughout the years.<br /> 3. Mummy the Curse. I feel an irrational attraction to this game. My gaming group is afraid of it... There couldn't possibly be a connection... could there?<br /> 4. Pathfinder. So many worlds to visit, so little time...<br /> 5. Trinity. Tough one. I will use the rest of my glue and claim all three eras are just chapters of one huge book.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I'm not sure I could live without any of my RPG books. I will fight ferociously against any who would harm my precious books. Precious... all of them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T04:02:49-07:00","id":253209,"title":"","content":"So you are only allowed to own five RPG core books. No supplements, nothing but the core. What 5 can you not live without?<br /> <br /> In no particular order:<br /> <br /> Vigil<br /> Blood and Smoke<br /> God-Machine Chronicle<br /> Dark Heresy<br /> WFRP 2nd edition","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thanke